        "text": "Step 1: To find the sum of the roots of \\( g(x) \\), we first need to understand how the transformation from \\( f(x) \\) to \\( g(x) \\) affects the roots. The function \\( g(x) = f(x + 5) \\) shifts the graph of \\( f(x) \\) to the left by 5 units. This means that if \\( r \\) is a root of \\( f(x) \\), then \\( r - 5 \\) is a root of \\( g(x) \\)."
      },
